{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779139929,"nonce":"yXgVabf/pr1ioN1e6/hWdiN/l4o=","title":"Refine Studio objective UI and selector targeting","message":"Follow-up to browser review on 5378a5d and correction issue 1177849.\n\nProblem:\n- Workspace duplicates entity lists between the left sidebar and main projection body.\n- The projection sidebar repeats the currently selected entity even though the right inspector already owns selected detail.\n- Bottom shelf tabs use a different visual treatment than the top projection tabs.\n- Objective rows do not expose penalty/norm or temporal aggregation controls, so users cannot choose L1 vs L2 or final vs trajectory penalties from the Objectives view.\n- Legacy/probe objective terms such as network activity are not mapped back to graph ports when a corresponding port selector exists, so the Graph view does not mark the penalized port.\n- Port-level objective creation still lacks a local action affordance such as a context menu.\n\nScope:\n- Remove duplicated workspace entity list/detail surfaces.\n- Restyle bottom shelf navigation to match the top tab treatment.\n- Add penalty and temporal controls to objective authoring/inspection and lowering.\n- Add a right-click graph-port action to add an objective from that port.\n- Normalize known seeded legacy objective selectors to graph ports where the model graph exposes the matching variable.\n- Analyze but do not fully solve nested substate browsing; cross-link to the state browser issue for runtime tree/index selection.\n\nVerification:\n- Focused scenario/objective tests.\n- npm run build.\n- Browser smoke on the seeded reaching task and RLRMP examples.","files":null}]}